     {
      "approval_id": "${a3}",
      "decision": "allow_once"
     }
    ]
   }
  }
 ],
 "note": "Appendix §G at a non-zero clock. c1 holds the lease from t=0 (deadline 15000) and has terminal input queued at the writer under epoch 1. At t=6000 c1 itself answers (its lease_epoch is ignored) and at t=9000 c2, a non-holder, answers: neither renews, grants or fences anything (no lease_changed, no session_changed). Without renewing, c1's repeat acquire at t=9000 returns the same epoch with ms_left 6000 (the deadline is still 15000, it was not reset by either answer), the queued input is written, not dropped, and the lease expires exactly at 15000. With nobody holding the lease, c2 answers a third prompt: accepted and handed over, and no lease is granted."
}
